    "correctness_assessment": "Guard checks actual PostgreSQL isolation and actual driver autocommit. For current psycopg driver, READ COMMITTED retention preserves later command fresh snapshots, source/child atomic completion and claim-token CAS; fallback rollback preserves other tested dialect/isolation paths.",
    "caveats": [
      "The earlier PostgreSQL/SQLite protocol receipts cover cached guard, not this exact effective guard; exact version should reuse meaningful protocol tests before production promotion.",
      "Driver autocommit property is present on current psycopg/psycopg2; defaultFalse for unknown PostgreSQL drivers should not imply universal compatibility.",
      "One extra get_isolation_level SQL roundtrip per task is included in prestart and may offset transaction/cache savings under real load.",
      "Longer connection checkout and idle read transaction/table locks during Django/SMTP increase connection footprint and susceptibility to idle-in-transaction timeout/DDL waits."
    ],
